{title: Jesus! The Name High over All}
{artist: Charles Wesley / Johann Crüger}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{tempo: 140}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (This arrangement is conflated from two sources: (1) United Methodist Hymnal (Nashville, Tennessee: United Methodist Publishing House, 1989), # 266, and (2) The )}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Je[Am]sus! the [C]name [Am]high [G]over [D]all,
[G]In hell or earth__[D7]__ or [G]sky;
[G]Angels and [C]men [G]before it [D]fall,
[Bm]And [Em]de[Am]vils [G]fear [D7]and [G]fly.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Je[Am]sus! the [C]name [Am]to [G]sinners [D]dear,
[G]The name to sin__[D7]__ners [G]giv’n;
[G]It scatters [C]all [G]their guilty [D]fear,
[Bm]It [Em]turns [Am]their [G]hell [D7]to [G]Heav’n.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]O [Am]that man[C]kind [Am]might [G]taste and [D]see
[G]The riches of__[D7]__ His [G]grace!
[G]The arms of [C]love [G]that compass [D]me
[Bm]Would [Em]all [Am]the [G]world [D7]em[G]brace.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 8}
[G]Hap[Am]py, if [C]with [Am]my [G]latest [D]breath
[G]I may but gasp__[D7]__ His [G]name,
[G]Preach Him to [C]all [G]and cry in [D]death,
[Bm]Be[Em]hold, [Am]be[G]hold [D7]the [G]Lamb!
{end_of_verse}
